@meeting careerLetGo
// Head writer 4: being let go, the day before you leave. Calder in her office: the Chief's last words. Straight,
// sorry, not cold. "Your note isn't finished" is her list of every junior/tech, with a note on each (canon).
title: The Chief's office
from: Chief Ines Calder
gist: Chief Calder: the Wren is letting you go. The Tern leaves tomorrow.
== lines
calder: Sit. Please.
calder > you: I'll say it straight, because you'd want that. The Wren is letting you go.
calder: The Tern leaves tomorrow. You'll be on it.
calder: This isn't about who you are. It's the shifts. Only the shifts.
calder: I keep a note on every tech I've trained. Yours isn't finished. That's the part I mind.
calder > you: Anything you want to say?   [listen]
? choice
* I'm sorry.   rel:calder+1
  calder: I know. So am I.
* Thank you for trying.   rel:calder+1
  calder: You're welcome. I'd try again.
* (Say nothing)
  calder: Fine. Quiet's fine.
calder: Wherever you go next, turn up. That's most of it. The rest you can learn.
calder: Go and say your goodbyes. People will want to.   [nod]
